/-!
# Inductive types on the step

A type given by constructors is a region of rows on the tree's first-order step, written by parties
with rights and installed schemas. Three facts, each with its own condition:

* **membership** (`Facts.membership`): every row of the region in every state reached from a state
  whose rows of the region are generated (the empty store among them) is generated by the
  constructors, when every party writes the type only through its constructors (`Facts.Writes`);
  several writers are allowed (`Numbers.twoWriters_membership`). The exact need is that every row
  written is generated (`Numbers.withShortcut_membership`);
* **induction** (`Facts.induction`): a property closed under the constructors holds of every row of
  the region in every state reached from the empty store, as an invariant of runs; the same
  condition;
* **closure** ("these and no others", a refutation by none queries): every closure statement survives every
  other party exactly when the region is owned (`Facts.closure_of_soleSender`, with
  `ThatsAll.closedReadingSurvives_iff_owned`); a given closure statement survives a writer through
  the constructors exactly when its list is closed under them (`Facts.survives_iff_ruleClosedIn`). A
  second writer through the constructors keeps membership and induction and breaks a closure
  statement (`Numbers.twoWriters_breaks_closure`); a writer that does not follow the constructors breaks
  induction on a named property (`Numbers.withJunk_breaks_induction`).

Every generated row is reached by a run (`Facts.reachable_of_generated`). Lists of numbers are a type
only together with the numbers they read, and the facts compose along reads (`Lists`). Addition by
structural recursion finishes within a bound read from the stage and answers the value
(`Recursion.addition_on_generated`), the value the model's addition computes on the same numbers
(`Agreement.answer_agrees`); the generated rows are the readings of the model's closed canonical
numbers (`Agreement.generated_iff_closedCanonical`, by the construction of a reading defined on
numerals only). Against a total reading of every content, junk included, a row is generated exactly
when its translation is typed at `num` and in canonical form (`Translation.generated_iff_translate`),
and the junk row's translation is typed at no type (`Translation.junk_untranslatable`). By
canonicity of the model's numbers (`Agreement.canonicity`), every closed term of `num` is equal to
the reading of exactly one generated row (`Agreement.closed_term_has_row`). On closed rows an indexed family is its extrinsic
description and each row has one derivation (`Families`). The type is the tree's provenance closure of
its constructor schemas (`ProvenanceBridge.derivable_iff_generated`). A guard on every made row is a
second mechanism for membership, for any rule set, at the price of a check of each row
(`Guards.guarded_membership`).
-/
